{#-
  xform-connections.json.j2 — advertised connection settings for the xform
  panel (SPEC §7, xform lifecycle).

  The panel never infers a public client view from the xray listener
  (upstream SPEC §3.2: NAT, TLS termination and reverse proxies make that
  inference unsafe — forpost's inbound sits behind the nginx SNI map), so
  the public view is advertised explicitly. One `direct` advertisement
  selects the `vless-reality` inbound and carries exactly the SPEC §8 link
  parameters: host = forpost.domain (the public nginx entry), port 443,
  tcp transport, reality security with SNI = forpost.server_name, the
  x25519 PUBLIC key (operator-derived once via `xray x25519 -i
  <private_key>` — the panel validates syntax but must not derive server
  material), and the FIRST short id.

  Upstream rejects duplicate inbound tags, so with backup_domain set the
  panel still advertises the primary name only — backup-name links remain
  the manual §8 contract.

  Rendered by create-forpost.yaml to /usr/local/etc/xform/connections.json
  (root:root 0644 — public link material only, no secrets). The panel
  watches the file's directory, so content-only updates apply live without
  a restart; XFORM_CONNECTIONS_CONFIG in xform.service.j2 must keep
  pointing at that path. tests/xform-connections.sh (run by the play after
  rendering, before any unit places a config) asserts the advertisement
  satisfies the inbound and that the env-var ⟺ path pair holds.
-#}
{%- set advertisement = {
  "inbound_tag": "vless-reality",
  "name": forpost.domain | mandatory("forpost is missing domain"),
  "topology": "direct",
  "host": forpost.domain | mandatory("forpost is missing domain"),
  "port": 443,
  "transport": {"type": "tcp"},
  "security": {
    "type": "reality",
    "fingerprint": "chrome",
    "server_name": forpost.server_name | mandatory("forpost is missing server_name"),
    "public_key": forpost.public_key | mandatory("forpost is missing public_key — derive it with: xray x25519 -i <private_key>"),
    "short_id": forpost.short_ids | first
  }
} -%}
{%- set connections = {"version": 1, "advertisements": [advertisement]} -%}
{{ connections | to_nice_json }}
